This is a fork of LibreOffice's libcdr with fixes made for the CorelDRAW
support of nitroview (https://github.com/gereoffy/jpeg-nitro), one commit
each (see git log since aaa57df): open paths not filled, text rotation,
horizontal stretch and bold, CMYK100 colours, hidden layers skipped, symbol
definitions not drawn as a page, transparent bitmap backgrounds, lost texts
of CorelDRAW 5 and 7-X5 files, and iconv instead of ICU. They were checked
against CorelDRAW's own PDF exports of real drawings.

libcdr is a library and a set of tools for reading and converting binary files
produced by Corel DRAW.

Most up to date code is available from Git repository at libreoffice.org
(https://gerrit.libreoffice.org/gitweb?p=libcdr.git), which is mirrored at
freedesktop.org (http://cgit.freedesktop.org/libreoffice/libcdr/). See
https://wiki.documentfoundation.org/DLP/Libraries/libcdr for more information.

libcdr requires boost, iconv, lcms2, librevenge and zlib to build.

The library is available under MPL 2.0.

Corel DRAW is a trademark by Corel. The developers of libcdr are in no way
affiliated with the company.
